<details class="mdrawer" data-screen-label="Methodology drawer">
  <summary>Methodology — how The Receipts work <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
  <div class="mdrawer-body">
    <div>
      <h3>The rules</h3>
      <p>Every number has a source. Every source has a date. Every model states its assumptions. Where a claim cannot be sourced, it is labeled an estimate, scenario, or hypothesis — never presented as fact.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Sources carry license, reuse status, and region coverage.</li>
        <li>Figures show visible &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; dates and a refresh cadence.</li>
        <li>Every correction is logged publicly.</li>
        <li>Negative results are published with the same prominence as wins.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Confidence labels</h3>
      <div class="u-37">
        <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--confirmed">Confirmed</span>
        <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--estimate">Estimate</span>
        <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--scenario">Scenario</span>
        <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--needs-refresh">Needs refresh</span>
      </div>
      <p>Derived figures — calculated from two or more sources — display every contributing source, never a single badge.</p>
      <p>Full methodology, the source register, and the corrections log: <a class="u-1" href="/receipts/">The Receipts</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

